{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"EVIDENCE FOR THIS PROPOSAL (2026-08-13): during a fleet pause, a do-not-submit hold on Gerrit change 1727 (stale revision carrying a silent compaction-suppression defect) was recorded in the holding session's session log and ticket comments — and a PEER session, following the standing both-+1s-submit rule, submitted it anyway. The record was correct and unread. A TTL'd fleet notice keyed to the change/ticket, surfaced at claim/review/submit time, is precisely the mechanism that would have prevented it. (Interim mitigation adopted: enforce holds on the change itself via Gerrit WIP status.)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786644477432081001,"uuid":"a376a0f5-a949-4237-a96d-132cf591f103"}